<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/8th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Arab siege of Constantinople</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">717–718 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as second Arab siege · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arab-byzantine-wars">Arab–Byzantine wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Arab siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> was a land and sea assault on the Byzantine capital by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> in 717–718 CE. The defenders under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-iii-the-isaurian">Emperor Leo III</a>, helped by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-fire">Greek fire</a>, a harsh winter and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgar</a> attacks, forced the Arab army to withdraw with heavy losses. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> profile treats its failure as a decisive check on Umayyad expansion into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-arab-siege-of-constantinople.jpg" alt="Second Arab siege of Constantinople" width="320" height="175" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 47-manasses-chronicle.jpg: Original: Constantine Manasses derivative work: Stegop · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:47-cropped-manasses-chronicle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
